    {
      "id": "e0011",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1370,
      "y": 46,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 192.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 87109,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1152019,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The type is assigned when the entry is written.\nDispatch is a lookup, not a judgment call.\n\n  COMPOUND    carries more than one thought   -> Split\n  QUESTION    asks for something not present  -> Recall\n  INFO        asserts something               -> Substantiate\n  OPEN SPLIT  has live children               -> Merge\n\nAn entry whose type cannot be assigned is a COMPOUND by\ndefault and gets Split. Splitting an atom is cheap; running\nSubstantiate on a compound is not.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "e0010",
      "originalText": "The type is assigned when the entry is written.\nDispatch is a lookup, not a judgment call.\n\n  COMPOUND    carries more than one thought   -> Split\n  QUESTION    asks for something not present  -> Recall\n  INFO        asserts something               -> Substantiate\n  OPEN SPLIT  has live children               -> Merge\n\nAn entry whose type cannot be assigned is a COMPOUND by\ndefault and gets Split. Splitting an atom is cheap; running\nSubstantiate on a compound is not.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false
    },
