    },
    {
      "id": "e0070",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10,
      "y": 1076.5,
      "width": 1220,
      "height": 280.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 554330,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7331030,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Major vs TOT. As written the difference is depth alone, which makes one\n   of the two names redundant. Either give Major a property TOT lacks, or\n   collapse to one name plus a depth field.\n\n2. Nothing commits. Recall fetches, Substantiate checks, Split divides,\n   Merge composes. No primitive takes a position. If that is deliberate,\n   say so, so the absence reads as a decision rather than a gap.\n\n3. Merge on contradiction Splits a new TOT, which can itself Merge into a\n   contradiction. That recursion needs a bound.\n\n4. Retry budgets. Split, Recall and Substantiate each loop. Is the budget\n   per-primitive, per-stream, or per-conversation?\n\n5. Confidence is produced by Substantiate and consumed by Merge. Nothing\n   says what scale it is on or how two of them compare.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "e0069",
      "originalText": "1. Major vs TOT. As written the difference is depth alone, which makes one\n   of the two names redundant. Either give Major a property TOT lacks, or\n   collapse to one name plus a depth field.\n\n2. Nothing commits. Recall fetches, Substantiate checks, Split divides,\n   Merge composes. No primitive takes a position. If that is deliberate,\n   say so, so the absence reads as a decision rather than a gap.\n\n3. Merge on contradiction Splits a new TOT, which can itself Merge into a\n   contradiction. That recursion needs a bound.\n\n4. Retry budgets. Split, Recall and Substantiate each loop. Is the budget\n   per-primitive, per-stream, or per-conversation?\n\n5. Confidence is produced by Substantiate and consumed by Merge. Nothing\n   says what scale it is on or how two of them compare.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false
    }
